<body>
<bookmark branch="index" id="bm_id3143272">
<bookmark_value>support on the Web</bookmark_value>
<bookmark_value>getting support</bookmark_value>
<bookmark_value>forums and support</bookmark_value>
<bookmark_value>Web support</bookmark_value>
</bookmark>
<section id="support">
  <h1 id="hd_id3146873"><variable id="00000001"><link href="text/shared/05/00000001.xhp">Getting Additional Support for %PRODUCTNAME</link></variable></h1>
  <description id="par_id3150667">You can find support on several %PRODUCTNAME service websites.</description>
</section>

<h2 id="hd_id191786403814118">Professional support</h2>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id271786403809027">Businesses, organisations and end users who need dedicated support contracts should visit our <link href="https://www.documentfoundation.org/professional-support/">Professional Support</link> page. </paragraph>

<h2 id="hd_id11786402490907">End-user community support (<link href="https://ask.libreoffice.org">https://ask.libreoffice.org</link>)</h2>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id481786402510179">This is a question-and-answer site available for multiple local language communities. It serves as a platform for sharing questions and answers. Please create a new topic for each question — one question with multiple possible answers. In most cases, answers come from users like you. Choose <menuitem>Help – Get Help Online</menuitem> to access the forum in your language.</paragraph>

<h2 id="hd_id311786402497522">Community discussion forum (<link href="https://community.documentfoundation.org/">https://community.documentfoundation.org/</link>)</h2>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id931786402945596">This is a forum for community general discussions related to %PRODUCTNAME and The Document Foundation.</paragraph>

<h2 id="hd_id2602967">%PRODUCTNAME End-user Documentation</h2>
<paragraph id="par_id3497211" role="paragraph">You can download documentation as PDF files, how-tos, and guides from the %PRODUCTNAME documentation website at <link href="https://books.libreoffice.org"><emph>books.libreoffice.org</emph></link>. You can also access the documentation website choosing the menu <menuitem>Help – User Guides</menuitem>.</paragraph>

<h2 id="hd_id321786407462280">%PRODUCTNAME FAQ</h2>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id881786407470915">A set of common questions that many users ask. Visit <link href="https://wiki.documentfoundation.org/Faq">https://wiki.documentfoundation.org/Faq</link>. </paragraph>

<h2 id="hd_id0804200803314150">Security</h2>
<paragraph id="par_id0804200803314235" role="paragraph">In case you are concerned about any security issue with using this software, you can contact the developers on the <link href="https://lists.freedesktop.org/mailman/listinfo/libreoffice">public mailing list</link>. If you want to discuss any issue with other users, send an email to the public mailing list <literal>users@global.libreoffice.org</literal>.</paragraph>

<h2 id="hd_id3168534">Downloads</h2>
<paragraph id="par_id3028143" role="paragraph">You can download the latest version of %PRODUCTNAME at <link href="https://www.libreoffice.org/download/">www.libreoffice.org/download/</link>.</paragraph>

<h2 id="hd_id911786407415083">The Document Foundation Wiki</h2>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id951786407430455">This wiki is maintained by the %PRODUCTNAME community. It mainly contains technical notes and guides for contributors, but also some documentation meant for users. Visit <link href="https://wiki.documentfoundation.org">https://wiki.documentfoundation.org</link></paragraph>

<h2 id="hd_id271786407436495">Developers Guide</h2>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id31786407452432">This manual describes how to write programs using the component technology UNO (Universal Network Objects) with LibreOffice. Visit <link href="https://wiki.documentfoundation.org/Documentation/DevGuide">https://wiki.documentfoundation.org/Documentation/DevGuide</link>.</paragraph>

<h2 id="hd_id0120200910361765">Participate and give back</h2>
<paragraph id="par_id0120200910361848" role="paragraph">If you want to take an active role in the worldwide %PRODUCTNAME community, you are very welcome to give feedback, discuss features, propose enhancements. To find the right contact point for contributing with your skills, visit <link href="https://whatcanidoforlibreoffice.org">https://whatcanidoforlibreoffice.org</link></paragraph>

<h2 id="hd_id601786408024370">Social Media</h2>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id811786441511628">Many social media and instant messaging groups are available for end users. Some of them are listed in
<link href="https://wiki.documentfoundation.org/Website/Web_Sites_services#Social_Media">https://wiki.documentfoundation.org/Website/Web_Sites_services#Social_Media</link></paragraph>

</body>
